Root cause:
The bounds check in cdc_ncm_rx_verify_ndp32() did not include the ndpoffset when validating the total size of the NDP32 and its DPE array against the skb length, leading to potential out-of-bounds read when the NDP32 is located near the end of the NTB.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
if ((sizeof(struct usb_cdc_ncm_ndp32) +
     ret * (sizeof(struct usb_cdc_ncm_dpe32))) > skb_in->len) {
```
Reason:
The bounds check compares only the computed size of the NDP32 header and DPE array directly against `skb_in->len`, without accounting for the `ndpoffset`. This allows out-of-bounds reads when the NDP32 is located near the end of the NTB, because the actual memory accessed (starting at `ndpoffset`) may extend beyond the total skb length.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
+	size_t ndp_len;
+	ndp_len = struct_size_t(struct usb_cdc_ncm_ndp32, dpe32, ret);
+	if (ndpoffset + ndp_len > skb_in->len) {
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a variable `ndp_len` computed using the safe `struct_size_t()` macro for the NDP structure with its DPE array. The new check adds `ndpoffset` to `ndp_len`, ensuring that the total memory range (from the start of the NDP to the end of its DPE array) does not exceed the skb length, thus preventing out-of-bounds reads.


